{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C", "description": "This file implements a CoAP (Constrained Application Protocol) client for sending USP (User Services Platform) messages over CoAP with support for DTLS encryption, message fragmentation, and retransmissions. It handles creating, connecting, managing, and tearing down CoAP connections, queuing outbound messages, processing incoming ACKs and RSTs, and managing retransmission logic with exponential backoff. It also manages SSL/TLS contexts, socket connections, and message fragmentation for reliable transfer of USP records to controllers.", "external_files": ["common_defs.h", "usp_coap.h", "usp_api.h", "usp-msg.pb-c.h", "msg_handler.h", "os_utils.h", "dllist.h", "dm_exec.h", "retry_wait.h", "text_utils.h", "nu_ipaddr.h", "iso8601.h"], "external_methods": ["DEVICE_SECURITY_CreateSSLContext", "DEVICE_LOCAL_AGENT_GetDualStackPreference", "tw_ulib_diags_lookup_host", "USP_LOG_Callstack", "SOCKET_SET_AddSocketToReceiveFrom", "SOCKET_SET_UpdateTimeout", "USP_PROTOCOL", "USP_LOG_Error", "USP_LOG_ErrorSSL", "USB_ASSERT", "USP_FREE", "USP_STRDUP", "TEXT_UTILS_SplitString", "TEXT_UTILS_PercentDecodeString", "STR_VECTOR_Destroy", "nu_ipaddr_from_str", "nu_ipaddr_to_sockaddr", "nu_ipaddr_str", "SSL_new", "SSL_free", "SSL_shutdown", "SSL_set_bio", "SSL_connect", "SSL_get_error"], "published": ["COAP_CLIENT_Init", "COAP_CLIENT_InitStart", "COAP_CLIENT_Destroy", "COAP_CLIENT_Start", "COAP_CLIENT_Stop", "COAP_CLIENT_AllowConnect", "COAP_CLIENT_UpdateAllSockSet", "COAP_CLIENT_ProcessAllSocketActivity", "COAP_CLIENT_QueueBinaryMessage", "COAP_CLIENT_AreAllResponsesSent"], "classes": [{"name": "coap_client_t", "description": "Represents a CoAP client connection to a controller, managing socket connection, SSL/TLS state, message queue, retransmission timers, and connection parameters."}, {"name": "coap_send_item_t", "description": "Represents a queued message (USP record) to be sent over a CoAP connection, including payload, destinati